    },
    "body": "ProcessBlock() stamps m_last_block_time only after ProcessNewBlock() returns, so getblockcount can show the new height, with nothing in flight, before the stamp is taken. A bumpmocktime in that gap stamps the block with the bumped time, and the final bump then leaves the ping timeout exactly at its boundary, where it never fires. Sync with a ping after the last block, so the node has finished processing it before the clock moves.\n\nThe race has been present since the test was added in #36080.\n\nFaling job: \nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/actions/runs/40589303246/job/122489039018",
